.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/pirates Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "Pirates [![Coverage][codecov-badge]][codecov-link]"
.PP
.SS "Properly hijack require"
This library allows to add custom require hooks, which do not interfere with other require hooks\&.

.PP
This library only works with commonJS\&.
.SH "Why?"
.PP
Two reasons:
.IP "1." 4
Babel and istanbul were breaking each other\&.
.IP "2." 4
Everyone seemed to re-invent the wheel on this, and everyone wanted a solution that was DRY, simple, easy to use, and made everything Just Work™, while allowing multiple require hooks, in a fashion similar to calling \fRsuper\fP\&.
.PP

.PP
For some context, see \fRthe Babel issue thread\fP which started this all, then \fRthe nyc issue thread\fP, where discussion was moved (as we began to discuss just using the code nyc had developed), and finally to \fR#1\fP where discussion was finally moved\&.
.SH "Installation"
.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install --save pirates
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
Using pirates is really easy: 
.PP
.nf
// my\-module/register\&.js
const addHook = require('pirates')\&.addHook;
// Or if you use ES modules
// import { addHook } from 'pirates';

function matcher(filename) {
  // Here, you can inspect the filename to determine if it should be hooked or
  // not\&. Just return a truthy/falsey\&. Files in node_modules are automatically ignored,
  // unless otherwise specified in options (see below)\&.

  // TODO: Implement your logic here
  return true;
}

const revert = addHook(
  (code, filename) => code\&.replace('@@foo', 'console\&.log(\\'foo\\');'),
  { exts: ['\&.js'], matcher }
);

// And later, if you want to un\-hook require, you can just do:
revert();

.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "pirates\&.addHook(hook, [opts={ [matcher: true], [exts: ['\&.js']], [ignoreNodeModules: true] }]);"
Add a require hook\&. \fRhook\fP must be a function that takes \fR(code, filename)\fP, and returns the modified code\&. \fRopts\fP is an optional options object\&. Available options are: \fRmatcher\fP, which is a function that accepts a filename, and returns a truthy value if the file should be hooked (defaults to a function that always returns true), falsey if otherwise; \fRexts\fP, which is an array of extensions to hook, they should begin with \fR\&.\fP (defaults to \fR['\&.js']\fP); \fRignoreNodeModules\fP, if true, any file in a \fRnode_modules\fP folder wont be hooked (the matcher also wont be called), if false, then the matcher will be called for any files in \fRnode_modules\fP (defaults to true)\&.
.SH "Projects that use Pirates"
.PP
See the \fRwiki page\fP\&. If you add Pirates to your project, (And you should! It works best if everyone uses it\&. Then we can have a happy world full of happy require hooks!), please add yourself to the wiki\&. 
